WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.300
Most actors would probably love a chance to
score a role in HBO's Game of Thrones, and

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.700
there've been plenty of A-list celebs who've
tried to get on the hit series to no avail.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.320
But there was a time when that wasn't the
case.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.680
Whether it was because of the grueling overseas
filming schedule, gripes with the cast's payscale,

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:23.530
or sheer confusion over the George R.R. Martin-inspired
story, here's a look at some actors who refused

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:24.820
Game of Thrones roles.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.600
Tamzin Merchant

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.460
Before Emilia Clarke gained international
fame as Daenerys Targaryen, Tamzin Merchant

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.360
was originally cast as the Mother of Dragons
for the show's original, unaired pilot.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.160
The first version of the pilot was, according
to showrunners D.B. Weiss and David Benioff,

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.260
a "massive problem," and 90 percent had to
be redone.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:49.640
"We had this great opportunity when HBO decided
to pick up the series despite, um, all of

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.780
the problems with the pilot.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.340
We got the chance to go back and rewrite it."

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.380
When HBO reshot, Merchant dropped out of the
project "for unknown reasons" and moved on

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:00.460
to Salem, opening the door for Clarke to take
over.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.160
Jennifer Ehle

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.620
Merchant wasn't the only original Game of
Thrones star to walk away after its early problems.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.320
Pride and Prejudice star Jennifer Ehle was
also in the original pilot, playing Catelyn

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:18.240
Stark, but she, too, walked away after the
first take spelled trouble, due to unavailability for the reshoots.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:23.740
She went on to star in films such as The King's
Speech, The Adjustment Bureau, and Zero Dark Thirty.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.560
She also nabbed a part in the television series
A Gifted Man, so her career hasn't really

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.920
been hurt by her decision to skip out on the
role that ultimately went to Michelle Fairley.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:34.980
Jamie Campbell Bower

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.420
Another actor featured in the original pilot
who had to drop out was Jamie Campbell Bower.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.540
The Twilight and Harry Potter actor was originally
cast for the role of Night's Watchman Waymar

00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:50.149
Royce in the scrapped pilot, but became unavailable
once reshoots were scheduled.

00:01:50.149 --> 00:01:54.549
Around the same time, the actor was starring
in the small screen series Camelot and readying

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:59.210
for a lead role in The Mortal Instruments,
so he was replaced by Rob Ostlere.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:03.169
It might not have made much of a difference
for his career anyway, since Royce was killed

00:02:03.169 --> 00:02:04.460
in the show's opening scene.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:05.980
Maybe that was an omen?

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:07.560
Brian Cox

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:13.260
Given his impressive resume, Scottish actor
Brian Cox might seem like a good fit for one

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.440
of the Seven Kingdoms, and somebody on the
show must've agreed — he admitted he was

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.100
once offered a role early on but turned it
down over the lack of loot.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:26.100
He told Vodzilla, "...stupidly, I turned it
down in the early days because they didn't

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.319
pay enough money.

00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:28.870
Now they have more money.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:29.870
And I was silly.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.220
I was silly, it was silly, because I'm a complete
addict now."

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:38.200
Cox admitted that he regrets missing out on
his chance, especially since it's featured

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.260
some of his old friends.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.640
He hopes he hasn't closed the door on that
opportunity for good.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.980
"I don't know what I could play.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:49.390
Maybe I could do — I mean, I just watched
my friend Ian McShane, and I thought, 'Ooh,

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.760
Ian's in it', so I settled down to watch him.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:56.820
And I thought, 'Ian did that?' and immediately
I thought, 'God, they must have paid him well,

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:57.780
because I know Ian!'

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:02.020
I'm still waiting for the call for Game of
Thrones and if they've got more decent money,

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:02.840
I'll be there!"

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:08.180
Hopefully they listen, because — seriously
— no one wants to be on the receiving end

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.620
of an angry Brian Cox.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.220
"And you, my friend, don't know crap about
life!

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:18.640
And why the f--- are you wasting my two precious
hours with your movie?"

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:20.580
Dominic West

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:25.889
While it's not quite known which Game of Thrones
role Dominic West was originally courted for,

00:03:25.889 --> 00:03:29.880
many suspect The Affair star may have been
asked to appear as Mance Rayder,

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:34.740
the former Night's Watchman who became known as "The King Beyond the Wall" for his affiliation

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:35.700
with the Free Folk.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:41.280
Whatever the role, though, West told Huffington
Post in 2012 that he had to decline the "lovely

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.980
part" because of family obligations.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.700
"I was offered something on Game of Thrones
and unfortunately, I hadn't seen it, but my

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.900
nephew and his father said, 'Gosh, Game of
Thrones is the only great show on!'

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.740
And I felt terrible, because I'd just turned
them down…

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.900
It was a lovely part, a good part.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.300
I'm going to regret it…

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.359
My problem is, I've got four kids, and at
the moment, I'm reluctant to be away from

00:04:02.359 --> 00:04:03.779
home for a long time.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.980
I can get a lot of work in London and still
be at home."

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.120
Gillian Anderson

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:14.800
X-Files star Gillian Anderson also had to
say "no thanks" to a chance at Game of Thrones

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.680
due to her obligations as a parent.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:23.080
She told Stylist Magazine in 2013, "Whether
it's Game Of Thrones or Downton Abbey, my

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.840
18-year-old cannot believe I've turned down
things she loves.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:30.300
But with a four and six-year-old, I can't
justify spending that kind of time away from

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.520
home, unless I'm working with [Martin] Scorsese."

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:37.520
While Anderson didn't share which role she
might've been offered, many speculate that,

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.720
due to her famous red locks, she may have
been a match for Melisandre the Red Witch.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.620
"There is someone I work with I like.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.320
His name is Jon Snow.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:47.420
But I'm not really sure he's the right guy."

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:48.280
"Why not?"

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:50.360
"I'm pretty sure he's dead."

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.040
Jonathan Pryce

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.520
Game of Thrones fans will undoubtedly recognize
Jonathan Pryce as the actor who portrayed

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.810
the duplicitous High Sparrow in Seasons 5
and 6.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:06.360
But believe it or not, he was actually asked
to join the show long before that — and turned it down.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:12.380
As he told BBC Radio 4, "I'd said no to the
very original series of Game of Thrones and

00:05:12.389 --> 00:05:16.630
all I did was flip through and look at the
names, look on these strange names, strange

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:19.160
dialogue and I thought 'Oh, it's not for me.'"

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.860
What changed his mind, he said, was the High
Sparrow's personality and presence.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.700
"High Sparrow, it's a great character.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:30.610
He comes into the story—everyone's well
established, the goodies and the baddies,

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:35.470
and they're all baddies in some shape or form—and
High Sparrow comes in as again quite relevant

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:39.860
because of the present Pope who presents himself
as a man of the people who'll get down washing

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:45.380
their feet and stuff … yet he is this incredibly
powerful figure who has the wherewithal to dispense justice."

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:47.880
Perdita Weeks

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.520
This one simply has to hurt.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:55.800
The Tudors and Penny Dreadful actress Perdita
Weeks was originally cast to star as Roslin

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.200
Frey, Edmure Tully's wife.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:01.740
But she backed out because her commitment
to another series called The Heretics required

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.420
her to be on location in Romania for six months.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:10.040
One problem: the Romanian government refused
to let them film, and the whole show got scrapped anyway.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:15.780
Weeks told The Daily Mail in 2012, "I gave
up a role on Game of Thrones to take the part

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:20.100
and even rang the producers to beg for it
back once I'd heard the news about Romania,

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:20.960
but it was too late."

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:26.200
The role was ultimately played by Alexandra
Dowling — although Weeks might not have

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.100
missed out on much.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:32.900
The character has appeared in just one episode
and was notably absent when her husband returned in Season 6.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:34.960
Ray Stevenson

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:40.060
Irish native Ray Stevenson was also given
a chance to star in Game of Thrones in its

00:06:40.069 --> 00:06:44.220
earliest episodes, but he told Movies.com
that he turned it down because he was simply

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:48.470
not into the TV scene at the time and that
he's not willing to join it now since it's

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.240
already too developed at this point.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.340
"I was offered [a role].

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:55.539
I also saw them before they even started,
very early on.

00:06:55.539 --> 00:06:57.620
I would rather have been [cast] at the beginning.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:01.419
I think it's wonderful, but it's not something
I would come into at this point.

00:07:01.419 --> 00:07:04.979
I don't know if I would add anything to it
at this stage … I would rather have been

00:07:04.979 --> 00:07:09.409
involved in the growth of a show, even though
everyone gets bumped off left, right and center.

00:07:09.409 --> 00:07:11.740
I kept seeing all the people I knew from Rome
in it!

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.139
But I can't, man!

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:13.820
I can't!"

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:19.319
Given that Stevenson joined both Dexter and
Black Sails in progress, though, it's possible

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:20.960
he could still change his mind.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:22.560
Lily Allen

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:27.420
According to singer Lily Allen, she turned
down the chance to star in Game of Thrones

00:07:27.439 --> 00:07:32.610
opposite her real-life brother Alfie Allen—she
would've been Yara Greyjoy to his Theon—because

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.980
of the ick factor associated with the roles.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:40.471
She wrote in a Reddit AMA in 2014, "I've been
asked to do a Game of Thrones cameo, they

00:07:40.471 --> 00:07:44.750
asked me if I'd be interested in playing Theon's
sister, and I felt uncomfortable because I

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.560
would have had to go on a horse and he would
have touched me up and s***.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.320
Once they told me what was entailed, I said
no thanks."

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.560
Then again, she may have been pulling the
Internet's leg that time.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:57.720
Her brother himself later came forward to
dispel her claim, telling Vulture that her

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:01.960
words weren't true and that Gemma Whalen was
always the original choice for the role.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:03.320
Thanks for watching!

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.500
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.040
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

